    "text": "Vision models trained on simple tasks that require aggregation of local information can learn global shortcuts, leading to failure in generalizing over task length or complexity.",
    "topic": "Length Generalization in Vision Models"
  },
  {
    "text": "Inspired by recent studies of length generalization in language models, the behavior of vision models trained on simple vision tasks that require the aggregation of local information across an image is examined.",
    "topic": "Vision Model Behavior"
  },
  {
    "text": "Similar to language models, vision models exhibit a tendency to exploit global shortcuts rather than relying on local information aggregation.",
    "topic": "Global Shortcuts in Vision Models"
  },
  {
    "text": "Vision Foundation Models induce a semantic manifold that constrains reconstruction within a specific semantic space, influencing generalization behavior.",
    "topic": "Semantic Manifold in Vision Foundation Models"
  },
  {
    "text": "GCPA constrains reconstruction within a semantic manifold induced by a Vision Foundation Model.",
    "topic": "GCPA and Semantic Manifold"
  }
]
